course: dictionary
lesson: 9004
title: Skid: sliding out of control
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A skid happens when something slides instead of gripping the ground. Context gives you the clues: «A layer of water between tyres and road makes a car skid.» Water makes the road slippery, so a car that slides is out of control. To skid means to slide sideways or forwards out of control.
explain: Read the next clue: «ABS anti-lock brakes notice when a wheel stops turning and skids.» A wheel that stops turning but keeps sliding along the road is not rolling. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "a wheel stops turning and slides out of control" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Skid can be a verb or a noun. As a verb it changes: skid, skids, skidded, skidding. As a noun it is a skid or skids, a sliding movement. Skids can also be strips of wood or metal under a heavy load, used to slide or rest it on.
fact: Skid means to slide sideways or forwards out of control, especially on ice, water or a smooth surface.
fact: Skidding happens when there is too little friction, so cars, bikes and people slide.
fact: That is why drivers slow down on ice and wet roads.
fact: «On the skids» is informal and means going badly, heading for failure.
fact: Skids are strips of wood or metal under a heavy load or helicopter, used to slide or rest it on.
exercise: «A layer of water between tyres and road makes a car skid.» What does skid mean here? | To shine brightly in the rain | To grow bigger | To stop neatly at a red light | *To slide out of control
exercise: Under a heavy load are two strips of wood, used to slide it along. What are they called? | *Skids | Treads | Tyres | Brakes
exercise: What is the past tense of skid? | *skidded | skids | skidding
test: The driver braked too hard on the wet road and the car began to skid. What does the car do? | Stops neatly at the kerb | Speeds up on purpose | Floats up into the air | *Slides out of control
test: What does «on the skids» mean? | Shining in the sun | Lying on a wooden board | Riding a sled downhill | *Going badly and heading for failure
exam: Skidding happens when there is too little friction. Why do drivers slow down on ice? | Because slow cars look nicer | Because ice makes cars lighter | *Because cars can slide out of control | Because ice makes tyres bigger
